# Errors

## Framework semantics

CakePHP maps exceptions to HTTP responses via error middleware and exception renderers (HTML/JSON). Controllers may translate expected domain outcomes to status codes; they should not swallow unexpected failures with empty catches.

## Required behavior

- Prefer framework exception rendering for unexpected errors.
- Map expected failures (not found, validation) to clear HTTP outcomes without hiding stack traces in production.
- Keep API error shapes consistent with project conventions (`viewClasses` / exception renderer).
- Do not catch `\Throwable` broadly just to return 200 with an error string.

## Anti-patterns

- Silent catch-all that hides failures
- Duplicating ad-hoc JSON error envelopes in every action when a renderer exists
- Leaking secrets/stack traces to clients in production

## Review checklist

- [ ] Unexpected errors flow through error middleware/renderer
- [ ] Expected domain failures use explicit status/body patterns
- [ ] Logs capture server-side detail without client leakage
